A||N||4||Bob Englert||Auto trans dipstick leak||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||04-06-2001||08:58 PM||||Just got back from a trip in my 87 GT and noticed a light film of oil on the back of the car.  I also saw a puddle after I parked it that seemed to be forming under the spot where the auto trans dipstick attaches to the transmission body.<P>Before I go take a close look, I was wondering how the dipstick is attached to the transmission body.  Are there gaskets that I can replace?  Any thoughts or suggestions are appreciated.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-06-2001||11:57 PM||||TH125 dipstick is in a rubber donut seal. It can be replaced. Try the parts stores but you will probably have to go to a tranny shop to get it.<P>pull out 1 bolt that hold the tube. pull the tube. pull the seal. put the new one in. put the tube back.<P>do this with a big oil pan under it. you will lose fluid doing this.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||04-07-2001||06:54 PM||||Thanks for the info.  <P>I got a good look at the leak today and it appears that the pan bolts were loose.  I can't seem to keep them tight.  I recently replaced the cork gasket with a rubber gasket but it keeps coming loose on me.<P>I might try to scratch alignment marks in the bolt heads so I can see if the bolts are loosening up or the gasket is compressing.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||04-08-2001||12:15 AM||||Remove each bolt, clean it and the hole with carb or brake cleaner, dry, drop of loc-tyte, reinstall bolt.......||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-08-2001||03:02 PM||||MAke sure it's the removable stuff and just a drop. other wise next time you have to work on the tranny you won't get them out without damaging the tranny case.||||reg||1
